  "register": "modern standard literary Russian in narration and educated speech; peasants and soldiers speak standard morphology with a whitelisted colloquial lexicon (design §7.2)",
  "orthography": {
    "policy": "modern (post-1918) orthography everywhere except the receptive pre-1918 texts of Глава 36",
    "yo": "ё is always written; a bare е in a lexeme whose form has ё is an error",
    "quotes": "«…» outer, „…“ inner",
    "dash": "— with spaces; direct speech by Russian punctuation rules",
    "numbers": "words for 1–10 and round numbers; digits for years and prices once G15 is taught; dates as digit chunks before G25"
  },
  "address": "ты in family, among soldiers, to animals and children; вы to Vera, the priest, the Orlovs, officers, and from Vera to adults; name + patronymic where a Russian would use it (taught in Глава 5); Order No. 1 forbids officers' ты to soldiers (Глава 32)",
